Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: Many medicines interact with prednisone.
Some change how much prednisone is in your body.
Others add to its side effects.
Tell your doctor about every medicine you take, including anything you start or stop during treatment.
Be especially careful with:
medicines that raise prednisone levels, such as ketoconazole, itraconazole, posaconazole, voriconazole, clarithromycin, and some HIV and hepatitis C medicines;
medicines that lower prednisone levels and can make it work less well, such as rifampin, rifabutin, rifapentine, carbamazepine, phenytoin, phenobarbital, primidone and St. John's wort;
NSAIDs and aspirin, which raise the risk of stomach ulcers and bleeding;
blood thinners such as warfarin, since prednisone can change how your blood clots and you may need extra monitoring;
insulin and diabetes tablets, since prednisone raises blood sugar and your doses may need to go up;
diuretics (water pills) and amphotericin B, which can lower potassium further;
digoxin, which is more likely to cause problems if your potassium is low;
live vaccines, which should usually be avoided;
Triplet: ["prednisone", "has interaction effect", "change how your blood clots and you may need extra monitoring"]

The relation 'has interaction effect' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug, when interacting with another substance, may cause the effect or outcome specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'interacts with': The subject drug has a drug interaction with the drug or substance specified by the object entity that may change effects or cause harm.
B. 'causes': The subject drug leads to or results in the effect or condition specified by the object entity.
C. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
D. 'affects': The subject drug influences or alters the function or levels of the chemical or entity specified by the object entity.
E. 'has effect in': The subject drug has a specific effect or behavior in the group of individuals specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
